 the orientation pledge to entering law classes.","evidence_claim":"Richardson Law reports that Chief Justice Mark Recktenwald administered the Law Student Pledge at orientation for 15 years, formally welcoming each entering class.","source_url":"https://law.hawaii.edu/29306/","source_title":"Honoring the Service and Partnership of Chief Justice Recktenwald","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-10-28","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Orientation ritual for entering Richardson Law students.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"richardson-ete-bowl","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Ete Bowl","title":"Cheer the Etes and Bruzers","subtitle":"William S. Richardson School of Law","notes":"Follow the annual flag-football matchup between current women law students, the Etes, and alumnae, the Bruzers; official scores run through 2025.","short_summary":"This law-school rivalry began in 1978 and continues as an alumni-student tradition.","evidence_claim":"Richardson Law documents the Ete Bowl as a 40-plus-year tradition, begun in 1978, between Etes and Bruzers.","source_url":"https://law.hawaii.edu/alumni/ete-bowl/","source_title":"Ete Bowl","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Participation and spectator details are organized by Richardson Law; play follows flag-football rules.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"richardson-stew-day","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Stew Day","title":"Meet Faculty in Chef Hats on Stew Day","subtitle":"William S. Richardson School of Law","notes":"Day-program law students can watch for the pre-finals meal when faculty and staff serve stew, desserts, and recognition of student kindness.","short_summary":"Faculty-created Stew Day pairs a free meal with stories of students helping one another.","evidence_claim":"UH News reports that Stew Day is a Richardson Law tradition launched in 2004, with faculty and staff serving a no-cost meal to day-program students.","source_url":"https://manoa.hawaii.edu/news/article.php?aId=8527","source_title":"UH Law School faculty, staff will serve hot meals to students as part of annual tradition","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2017-04-17","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"For full-time day JD students; offered by the law school around finals.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"richardson-noodle-night","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Noodle Night","title":"Join Noodle Night at Twilight","subtitle":"William S. Richardson School of Law","notes":"Evening-program law students can watch for the faculty-and-staff-served Noodle Night meal, the companion ritual to daytime Stew Day.","short_summary":"The evening JD program has its own no-cost pre-finals meal and faculty service line.","evidence_claim":"UH News identifies Noodle Night as an annual Richardson Law tradition in which faculty and staff serve a no-cost meal to evening part-time students.","source_url":"https://manoa.hawaii.edu/news/article.php?aId=8527","source_title":"UH Law School faculty, staff will serve hot meals to students as part of annual tradition","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2017-04-17","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"For Evening Part-Time Program students; traditionally scheduled around finals.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uh-manoa-filgrad","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"FilGrad Mānoa","title":"Celebrate at FilGrad Mānoa","subtitle":"Center for Philippine Studies","notes":"Graduating Filipinx students can look for the annual FilGrad ceremony, built around cultural recogni